course: dictionary
lesson: 10903
title: Words you can see
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Visibly means in a way that can be seen or noticed easily. Its root is visible, which means you can see it. Adding -ly tells you how something shows, so «she was visibly upset» means you could see that she was upset.
explain: Visibly is often used with feelings. «He was visibly nervous before the test» means his nerves showed on his face or in the way he moved. Writers use it to show a feeling without having to say it outright.
explain: Look at this context: «Hand gel does not clean well when hands are visibly dirty.» The dirt can be seen, so visibly fits. To check, ask yourself: could someone see it? If yes, your meaning works in the sentence.
fact: Visibly means in a way that can be seen or noticed easily.
fact: «She was visibly upset» means you could see that she was upset.
fact: Common phrases include «visibly shaken», «visibly tired» and «visibly improved».
fact: In science, «the plant had visibly grown» means you could see the change without measuring, though scientists still measure to be sure.
fact: Visible is the root word: if something is visible, it can be seen.
exercise: Ellie went pale and was «visibly nervous» before the show. What does visibly mean here? | *In a way that could be seen | In a quiet, secret way | Very slowly | In a loud, angry voice
exercise: «Hand gel does not clean well when hands are visibly dirty.» Find and copy the word that tells you the dirt can be seen. | hands | gel | clean | *visibly
exercise: Which word could replace visibly in «she was visibly upset» without changing the meaning much? | quietly | *clearly | sometimes | hardly
test: Dad was visibly tired after work. What does this show? | He was secretly tired and hid it | He was happy and bouncy | *You can see he was tired | He slept all day
test: «The plant had visibly grown in a week.» What does visibly mean? | *The change could be seen without measuring | The plant was made of paper | The plant had grown in secret | The plant was hidden from view
exam: Which sentence uses visibly correctly? | *The old bridge was visibly cracked, so you could see the damage | The bridge visibly sang a song | The bridge was visibly invisible in the fog | The bridge was visibly quiet at night
